WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.553
Idea. Think about a shoe shop. A five-year-old, a teenage footballer and a grandparent all need shoes, but each of them wants something very different.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:19.590
Dividing a market into groups of customers who share similar characteristics is called market segmentation. Each group is a market segment.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:29.535
Choosing which segment to aim your products and promotion at is called targeting. Then the business fits its product, price and promotion to that group.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:46.287
Method. Step one: choose a basis for splitting customers. Common bases are age, income, location, lifestyle and demographics. Demographics means features of the population, such as age, gender and family type.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:57.212
Step two: describe what one segment needs, using facts from the case. Step three: link targeting to a product, price or promotion that fits that need.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:07.293
Step four: end with the result for the business. More sales, more loyal customers, or less money wasted promoting to people who will never buy.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:24.867
Worked example. Here is a real question from Paper one in November 2023. Explain one benefit to a business of using market segmentation to target its customers. It is worth three marks: one benefit, then two linked steps.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:35.891
Mark one is the benefit. Segmentation lets the business find groups of customers who share similar characteristics, such as the same age or income.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:45.333
Mark two explains why that helps. The business can design a product, set a price and choose promotion that match exactly what that group wants.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:55.913
Mark three gives the result. Because the product suits them better, those customers are more likely to buy and to come back, so sales and loyalty rise.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:07.969
Common mistake. Mistake one: confusing segmentation with market research. Research collects information. Segmentation divides customers into groups.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:16.484
Mistake two: naming a basis but not using it. Say how this business would use the basis, and what happens as a result.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:32.028
Your turn. Now you try. A sports drink company sells one drink to everyone. Identify one basis it could use to segment its market, and explain one benefit of targeting one segment. Pause and decide.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:47.830
Answer. One good answer uses age. Target teenagers who play sport. Sell smaller bottles at a lower price and promote them on social media. The drink suits them better, so more teenagers buy it and sales rise.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:59.726
That is the pattern for every answer on this type: group the customers, fit the product, price and promotion to them, then show the result. Now try the practice questions.
